WEBVTT

00:00:00.638 --> 00:00:04.308
Here is how to install RoonPilot directly in your browser

00:00:04.588 --> 00:00:07.870
We will go through every click together including how to

00:00:07.762 --> 00:00:09.995
connect the correct USB device

00:00:11.888 --> 00:00:15.882
You need your RoonPilot a USB data cable and Chrome

00:00:15.875 --> 00:00:19.358
or Edge on a computer A charging-only cable will not

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:23.033
work Connect the device directly to your computer

00:00:24.933 --> 00:00:29.766
This installation erases the existing settings on RoonPilot If you

00:00:29.658 --> 00:00:33.828
still need them save a configuration backup first If your

00:00:33.721 --> 00:00:37.141
device is brand new you can continue straight away

00:00:39.017 --> 00:00:42.649
Open Chrome or Edge Enter the address shown here in

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:46.087
the address bar then press Enter This takes you to

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:48.112
the official RoonPilot installer

00:00:49.975 --> 00:00:54.395
Scroll down to Choose firmware Leave the current USB version

00:00:54.288 --> 00:00:58.470
selected In this example it is version two point zero

00:00:58.363 --> 00:01:02.070
point two A newer version may be available later

00:01:03.946 --> 00:01:07.691
Scroll down a little further Read the notices about the

00:01:07.583 --> 00:01:12.353
correct processor erasing the device and the licence Tick both

00:01:12.246 --> 00:01:15.753
boxes You can now click Install RoonPilot

00:01:17.679 --> 00:01:20.637
The device name is what matters not the number in

00:01:20.529 --> 00:01:25.024
brackets The entry highlighted in green is correct If you

00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:29.124
already see it connect directly The next steps are only

00:01:29.017 --> 00:01:31.862
needed if USB serial appears instead

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:37.895
Sometimes the list only shows USB serial That is the

00:01:37.788 --> 00:01:42.358
other processor inside the device Do not select it You

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:45.395
only need to turn over the USB-C connector at the

00:01:45.288 --> 00:01:46.282
RoonPilot

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:52.299
Leave the device selection window open Unplug the cable at

00:01:52.192 --> 00:01:56.312
the RoonPilot Leave the other end connected to your computer

00:01:56.567 --> 00:01:59.137
The old entry disappears from the list

00:02:01.017 --> 00:02:05.099
Turn the unplugged connector around its own lengthwise axis by

00:02:04.992 --> 00:02:08.324
one hundred and eighty degrees The side that was facing

00:02:08.217 --> 00:02:11.812
upwards is now underneath You do not need a different

00:02:11.704 --> 00:02:12.387
cable

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:18.099
Plug it back into the same socket The browser updates

00:02:17.992 --> 00:02:22.212
the list The correct device name now appears Click that

00:02:22.104 --> 00:02:24.099
entry then click Connect

00:02:25.988 --> 00:02:30.783
After connecting a small RoonPilot window opens Click Install

00:02:30.675 --> 00:02:34.320
RoonPilot You do not need Logs and Console for a

00:02:34.213 --> 00:02:35.558
normal installation

00:02:37.471 --> 00:02:41.528
This window asks you to confirm the installation The warning

00:02:41.421 --> 00:02:44.491
means that all data on the device will be erased

00:02:44.771 --> 00:02:46.991
When you are ready click Install

00:02:48.875 --> 00:02:52.933
First the installer prepares the device and erases its memory

00:02:53.213 --> 00:02:57.445
Then the percentage increases Keep the window visible and leave

00:02:57.338 --> 00:03:01.245
the cable connected The actual installation may take a few

00:03:01.138 --> 00:03:01.858
minutes

00:03:04.888 --> 00:03:09.020
Wait until you see Installation complete Only then is the

00:03:08.913 --> 00:03:13.458
installation finished Click Next then close the small window

00:03:13.725 --> 00:03:18.508
RoonPilot restarts Leave USB connected to keep it powered

00:03:20.429 --> 00:03:24.812
The RoonPilot screen now shows Wi-Fi setup Open the Wi-Fi

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:29.524
list on your phone tablet or laptop Connect to RoonPilot

00:03:29.417 --> 00:03:34.162
Setup The last six characters identify your particular device

00:03:36.054 --> 00:03:40.112
The password is roonpilot a hyphen then setup all in

00:03:40.004 --> 00:03:44.249
lower case If your phone reports no internet stay connected

00:03:44.142 --> 00:03:47.424
anyway This network is only used to set up the

00:03:47.317 --> 00:03:48.112
device

00:03:49.988 --> 00:03:53.558
Open your browser and enter one nine two dot one

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:59.245
six eight dot four dot one If necessary choose English

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:03.208
Enter your home Wi-Fi name and password Use a two

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:07.195
point four gigahertz network Click Save and restart

00:04:09.083 --> 00:04:13.678
Reconnect your phone to your home Wi-Fi RoonPilot now searches

00:04:13.571 --> 00:04:16.553
for your running Roon Server When it is waiting for

00:04:16.446 --> 00:04:22.003
authorisation open Settings and Extensions in Roon Enable RoonPilot

00:04:21.896 --> 00:04:23.141
by Senior Coder

00:04:25.042 --> 00:04:28.824
Finally choose the zone you want to control directly on

00:04:28.717 --> 00:04:32.874
the RoonPilot screen Once the player view appears setup is

00:04:32.767 --> 00:04:35.774
complete Enjoy using RoonPilot

00:04:37.679 --> 00:04:41.562
If no USB device appears first check your data cable

00:04:41.842 --> 00:04:45.262
If the installer reports that your ESP thirty-two board is

00:04:45.154 --> 00:04:48.949
not supported turn the connector over as shown then start

00:04:48.842 --> 00:04:50.312
the connection process again

00:04:52.221 --> 00:04:55.828
You can repeat any step using the chapters The full

00:04:55.721 --> 00:04:59.416
written guide is available on the RoonPilot project page
